learning_outcomes:
  - Recognise when intellectual property law applies to a digital scenario, including software, creative works, brand identity and commissioned design
  - Distinguish copyright, patents, trade marks and database right, and identify which regime is engaged in a given scenario
  - Explain why copyright in commissioned work generally stays with the creator absent a written assignment
  - Recognise that open-source software is copyrighted, not public domain, and that open-source licences are enforceable as copyright licences
